# Python documentation (Writer)

When adding or changing Python code under `src/`:

- Every module must have a module-level docstring (purpose, main entry points).
- Every public function must have a docstring with a one-line summary, `Args`, `Returns`, and `Raises` when applicable.
- Private helpers (`_name`) must have at least a one-line docstring explaining behavior.
- Non-obvious module constants should have an inline comment or live in a documented block.
- Keep docstrings accurate when behavior changes.

Prefer Google-style docstrings. Do not leave stub UI or placeholder handlers undocumented—note if they are stubs.
